  "tolerance_rationale": {
    "ols": "Well-conditioned rational arithmetic has tight floating-point gates; Longley is ill-conditioned and NIST provides roughly 15 certified significant digits, so require eight-digit relative agreement.",
    "perfect_fit": "Exact zero RSS needs an absolute gate, not relative error; require sigma2 <= 1e-14 and coefficient absolute error <= 1e-8.",
    "balanced_lmm": "Variance estimates are optimized numerically; allow two parts per million while checking independently derived ML/REML optima and likelihood criteria. Finite-difference Satterthwaite degrees of freedom have a separately declared absolute gate of 0.05 against the exact balanced-model identity.",
    "paper_examples": "Initial gates target three significant digits for optimizer-dependent quantities; this is selected example agreement, not bitwise or historical-binary reproduction. Zero/small parameters also have a 3e-4 absolute gate. Inference probabilities use an absolute 1e-5 gate. Numerical review may replace contracts through a new registry revision, never silently after a failed run."
  },
